      "content": "the last thing i want to do is sound like i'm just bashing tech, but it really feels like we're at a breaking point where these companies are just too powerful for democracy to function properly. if we don't actually break them up or force them to open up their data, aren't we basically just accepting that a handful of CEOs get to decide the future of how we all live and communicate? like, is there actually any realistic way for a fair market to exist if they aren't forcibly restructured?",
